/ A format type owns its parse (ruling 5): the first read into a json file parses it
/ into a plang dict. The read goes first (decision 401 — json stays text until read into),
/ then `%cfg% is dict` is true. Today's parse yields a C# JsonElement, so `is dict` reads
/ false even after a successful member read (Cut2 / Narrow baseline).
ReadIntoIsADict
- read config.json, write to %cfg%
- assert.equals(Expected="two", Actual=%cfg.alpha%, Message="the first read goes through the json type")
- condition.if(Left=%cfg%, Operator="is", Right="dict") { variable.set(Name=%isDict%, Value=true) }
- assert.equals(Expected=true, Actual=%isDict%, Message="after the read, %cfg% is a plang dict")
